	(text "Bias-T supply (D-54). U1001 PCA9539 at 0x77 (A1 A0 = 11), on the same bus and RESET (= RLY_EN) as U901 to U903.\nIO0_0..3 = A1..A4_BIAS_EN (outputs, active high), IO0_4..7 = A1..A4_BIAS_OK (inputs), IO1 spare, held low by RN1001, RN1002 (D-121).\nPer feed: +12V_AUX, 10R sense, IRFL9014 P-MOSFET high side, BC857B limiter (about 42 to 78 mA over temperature), BSS138BK gate drive.\nA short on the coax holds the feed in current limit: 0.8 W max in the P-MOSFET, Tj about 103 C at 55 C ambient on 1 sq. inch copper (C-17).\nThe firmware switches a feed off when EN is high and OK stays low (fault), and reports it. OK changes raise EXP_INT.\nSafe state: RLY_EN low holds U1001 in reset, the 100k pull-downs keep every feed off (KILL also turns the preamps off).\nAk_BIAS goes to the bias-T of antenna port Ak (L2, C2 DNP there; fit on a bias-T port only)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 190.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "88e3cd7c-3bc2-5fa7-9e85-20062b4ad82e")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 45.72 60.96)
		(end 127.0 137.16)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "88116669-b91d-55fd-8d3c-80bbd2197ed3")
	)
